{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784538070,"nonce":"Qn78noUIq96RB4JVSSqCUjqeXGU=","title":"[adr-0056] Read model: cascade cause + superseded/shadowed derivation","message":"Amends ADR-0056 (2026-07-20 amendment). All client-side in ui/scarab-web-ui/src/takes.ts — no engine change.\n\n- Add 'cascade' to AttemptCause: an attempt armed by a RunRestartRequested whose TARGET is this step = 'rerun'; armed only via the invalidated[] set (not the target) = 'cascade'. Today attemptCauses() tags both 'restart'.\n- Rename 'restart' cause -\u003e 'rerun' (user-facing verb).\n- Derive 'superseded': AttemptStarted with no matching AttemptFinished whose step is re-armed by a LATER RunRestartRequested (was running, cut short). Distinct from cancelled/failed.\n- Derive 'shadowed': a succeeded attempt that is not the latest-successful (of-record) one for its step.\n- replayTake straddler classification: an invalidated in-flight step at the boundary is 'superseded', not 'never finished (0)'.\n\nAcceptance: unit-level derivation matches the ADR taxonomy for the diamond a-\u003eb-\u003e{c,d}-\u003ee with a rerun of b while c is in-flight.","files":null}]}